<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9256] SQL: make sure that fetched results are cleared from iterator when last element is fetched</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9256</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In practice it is possible for user to forget to nullify Ignite&apos;s result set after iteration is finished. Or he may delay cleanup for some reason. &lt;br/&gt;
The problem is that we hold the whole H2&apos;s result set inside our iterator even after all results are delivered to the user. &lt;br/&gt;
We should forcibly close and then nullify all H2 objects once all results are returned. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Key code pieces:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;IgniteH2Indexing.executeSqlQueryWithTimer&lt;/tt&gt; - how we get result from H2&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;H2ResultSetIterator&lt;/tt&gt; - base iterator with H2 objects inside&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13178560">IGNITE-9256</key>
